# Line-ending conversion must never touch a binary fixture.
#
# core.autocrlf is on for most Windows checkouts, and git decides text-vs-binary
# by looking for NUL bytes in the first 8000. A .docx or a .ttf is full of them
# and is detected correctly. A PDF is not: juan-rivera.pdf is 2.4KB of ASCII85
# with no NUL anywhere, so git called it text and rewrote its 67 LF bytes to
# CRLF on checkout -- 2367 bytes in the repository, 2434 in a fresh clone, with
# the ASCII85 stream and every xref offset broken.
#
# Nothing caught it because the file was only ever WRITTEN here, never checked
# out again; it corrupts on clone, so it would have failed for the first person
# who cloned the repository and ran the tests, and for nobody working in it.
#
# Marked by extension rather than by path so a new fixture is safe by default.

*.pdf   binary
*.docx  binary
*.ttf   binary
*.png   binary
*.zip   binary
*.ico   binary
